Open up runtime.setResolution on the local-control surface so the operator can
drive Sunshine's operation-3 path through the same JSON-RPC contract used for
bitrate and FPS. Sunshine currently advertises SET_RESOLUTION as a
proof-gated operation for the validated Korri profile; this patch exposes it
when either the supported or proof-gated capability bit is set so the explicit
proof-gated override can reach the sender path while unsupported sessions still
fail closed.

Acceptance of the request still relies on Sunshine's own bounds + same-aspect
check; this patch widens the client-side gate and threads
secondaryValue=height through the existing dispatcher.

